    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW28UshuPex7Q74iy2gXh676H)_\n\n## What\n- `:parent-of` / `:parent-prop` / `:except-prop` and the `:fold-tag` count now read **every** link in a meta value, not only the first.\n- Cause: `vulpea-note-meta-get-list` with type `link` runs one `string-match` per value, so `- pub-author :: [[id:a][A]], [[id:b][B]]` yields only `a`. Co-authors after the first never saw the work in their Works table. New helper `sp-collec-query--link-ids`.\n- Test added.\n\n## Notes\n- In the vault, 18 of 32 multi-author `incollection` notes were missing from a table versus 13 of 145 single-author ones; this explains the multi-author part, not the single-author misses.\n- No CHANGELOG edit. Tested in Emacs 29.3 with stubs, not on the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD49hEeJCwd214jHzL)_",
